 r←key ParseDependencySetting ref;name;targetKey;value;hasTargetKey;folder;target;msg
⍝ Takes a "tatin" or "nuget" dependency setting from the namespace `ref`, splits it into folder and target namespace, and checks it.
⍝ This is the only function that knows how such a setting is written: all other code works with its result.
⍝ `key` names the setting, e.g. 'dependencies_dev.tatin'; the part after the dot is the name looked up in `ref`.
⍝ `ref` is a dependency namespace such as `config.CIDER.dependencies`; use `GetDependencyNamespace` to get one.
⍝ A setting comes in one of two forms:
⍝ * The old form: "tatin" is '<folder>' or '<folder>=<namespace>', and there is no "tatinTarget".
⍝ * The new form: "tatin" is '<folder>' and "tatinTarget" is '<namespace>' or empty.
⍝ The same goes for "nuget" and "nugetTarget". Using both forms at once ('=' in "tatin" plus "tatinTarget") is an error.
⍝ An empty or missing folder means there is no such folder.
⍝ Blanks around the folder or in the target namespace are rejected rather than removed: they are typos.
⍝ Returns (msg folder target):
⍝ * `msg` is empty when the setting is valid; otherwise it says what is wrong, naming `key`.
⍝ * `folder` and `target` are empty when there is no folder or the setting is invalid.
⍝ * An empty `target` means the project space; otherwise `target` is relative to the project space.
 r←'' '' ''
 name←key↓⍨key⍳'.'
 targetKey←name,'Target'
 value←''
 :If 0<ref.⎕NC name
     value←,ref⍎name        ⍝ A one-character value from an APL caller is a scalar
 :EndIf
 hasTargetKey←0<ref.⎕NC targetKey
 :If hasTargetKey
     folder←value
     target←,ref⍎targetKey
     msg←'Something is wrong with "',key,'" (',value,') and "',key,'Target" (',target,'): '
 :Else
     folder←value↑⍨¯1+value⍳'='
     target←value↓⍨value⍳'='
     msg←'Something is wrong with "',key,'" (',value,'): '
 :EndIf
 :If 0=≢value,target
     :Return
 :EndIf
 :If hasTargetKey∧'='∊value
     msg,←'use either <folder>=<namespace> or "',name,'Target", not both'
 :ElseIf hasTargetKey∧0=≢folder
     msg,←'a target namespace needs a folder'
 :ElseIf 1<'='+.=value
     msg,←'expected <folder> or <folder>=<namespace>'
 :ElseIf ('='∊value)∧(0=≢folder)∨0=≢target
     msg,←'expected <folder> or <folder>=<namespace>'
 :ElseIf ','∊folder
     msg,←'only one folder is allowed'
 :ElseIf ' '∊(⊃folder),⊃⌽folder
     msg,←'the folder must not start or end with a blank'
 :ElseIf ' '∊target
     msg,←'the target namespace must not contain blanks'
 :ElseIf 0=≢target
     msg←''
 :ElseIf (⊃target)∊'#⎕'
     msg,←'the target namespace must be relative to the project space'
 :ElseIf 0≠⊃(⎕NS'').⎕NC target
     msg,←'"',target,'" is not a valid namespace name'
 :Else
     msg←''
 :EndIf
 :If 0=≢msg
     r←msg folder target
 :Else
     r←msg'' ''
 :EndIf
⍝Done
